<% content_for :title, "#{@title} / #{@site_name}" %>

<div class="layout">
  <aside class="col-left"></aside>

  <section class="col-main">
    <h2 class="section-title"><%= @title %></h2>

    <div class="panel static-page">
      <% case @slug %>
      <% when "about" %>
        <p><%= @site_name %> is a small, self-hosted social network built to look and
           behave like the classic web client from 2014&ndash;2016.</p>
        <p>Post short updates, follow people, favorite and retweet what you like, and
           message anyone directly. The first account created owns the instance and can
           moderate members, grant verified badges and adjust site settings.</p>
      <% when "help" %>
        <h3>Posting</h3>
        <p>Tweets are limited to <%= max_tweet_length %> characters. Use the box at the top
           of the home timeline to post. You can attach one image per tweet.</p>
        <h3>Following and followers</h3>
        <p>Open any profile and use the Follow button. Your own following and follower
           lists are on your profile under those tabs.</p>
        <h3>Direct messages</h3>
        <p>Use the Message button on a profile to start a private conversation. Existing
           conversations are listed under Messages.</p>
        <h3>Account settings</h3>
        <p>Change your display name, bio, links and photos, or set a new password, from
           the Settings page.</p>
      <% when "tos" %>
        <p>By using <%= @site_name %> you agree to follow the rules set by the operator of
           this instance.</p>
        <p>Do not post content that is unlawful, harassing, or designed to deceive other
           members. Accounts that break these rules may be suspended or banned.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for the content you post and for keeping your password
           secure.</p>
      <% when "privacy" %>
        <p><%= @site_name %> stores the account details you provide: your username, display
           name, email address, profile fields, posts, and the social actions you take.</p>
        <p>Your email address is never shown publicly. Your password is stored as a
           salted hash and is never kept in readable form.</p>
        <p>This instance is run by its own operator. Contact them with any privacy
           questions about this deployment.</p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="col-right"></aside>
</div>